rota lap 5038, row 3 -- Water tastes; read the file up close and ask what a second run changes. That question is what saved the lap: the first reading said both path spellings changed the emitted binary, and running one unchanged spelling twice showed a Debug build of this toolchain is not reproducible at all.
think Cold endurance run first, detached, cadence-slice 1: 304 read, 290 green, 12 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no. All twelve reds inherited -- eleven whole-tree population ratchets a peer breached, one dead-letter box at 46 stash entries.
think rye/src/main.rye fed the receipt key hasher.update(zig) and hasher.update(rye_lib) -- two path STRINGS -- beside the content hashes of both. A path names how an input was found rather than what it compiled.
think Measured before: one pinned compiler reached four ways spoke four keys and bought four full rebuilds. After: one key, four times.
think The measurement needed its own control. Comparing two spellings at -ODebug answered DIFFER for both, which reads exactly like the path decides the output. Running one spelling twice answered DIFFER too.
think At -OReleaseSmall the build is reproducible and both spellings emit byte-identical binaries. At -ODebug two builds of one source part in 45,027 of 10,239,778 bytes, entirely in anonymous struct serial numbers.
think The module header had always promised a key over five contents and no path. The doc was right; the code carried two inputs it never announced, and the control asserted the undocumented behavior as law.
obs Each new leg was bitten by its own mutant compiler -- one with only the toolchain path restored, one with only the library path. A hit leg proven in no direction cannot be told from a leg that always passes.
obs rune_assert_sweep has grown from one over its ceiling to five, on peers' Rye commits. rye/src/main.rye names all 16 of its asserts, so this lap could not lower it from the file it was in. Caravan holds 228 unnamed asserts across four modules and is this lane's.
obs The hot pass added two reds over the cold, both mine: shelving the elder account left one link at the card's depth. Following the refusal's own instruction -- run the repointer with --apply -- answered unknown argument at exit 2, and the family's witness recited 78 readings while its control emitted 76. Both halves were self-description and nothing held either. Booked at stamp 20260916.050900.
obs rune_assert_sweep read 6,492 against 6,487 when this lap measured it and 6,480 at a ceiling of 6,480 after the rebase, a peer having named both arrivals and folded %752 while this lap ran. The card carries the corrected reading rather than the one I measured.
obs The marker bump v5 to v6 buys legibility rather than safety -- a changed input set already misses -- and costs one rebuild per standing receipt, 96 on this ship.
